From: Abzu <abzu@localhost>
Date: Sat, 10 Oct 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 1/4] gui: honour GAFontAntialiasing defaults in NSFont attribute lookup

Abzu overlay (see ../README.md): map the documented Abzu default
-GAFontAntialiasing onto NSFont rendering so text matches Aqua-style
subpixel smoothing out of the box. gnustep-gui reads the font user-defaults
dictionary in _defaultAttributesForFontDescriptor; we override the
NSFontAntialias entry from the dedicated GA* default there, so desktop-wide
settings apply to every NSFont without app cooperation.

Upstreaming: tracked per-patch in docs/ROADMAP.md.

---
diff --git a/Source/NSFont.m b/Source/NSFont.m
index 6c692bc..14eb13e 100644
--- a/Source/NSFont.m
+++ b/Source/NSFont.m
@@ -5,6 +5,12 @@
     {
       NSMutableDictionary *d = [[UserDefaults dictionaryForKey: GSFontKey]
 				      mutableCopy];
+      /* Abzu overlay: -GAFontAntialiasing (bool, default YES) takes
+       * precedence over the generic GSFontKey dictionary so desktop-wide
+       * smoothing applies to every NSFont without app cooperation. */
+      [d setObject: ([UserDefaults boolForKey: @"-GAFontAntialiasing"]
+					? @"YES" : @"NO")
+				forKey: NSFontAntialias];
       if (nil != fd)
 	{
 	  /* Merge any font descriptor attributes into the defaults. */
